                "markdown": "A non-empty global tool allowlist applied uniformly to a mix of public and private inbound channels, with no channel-specific restriction narrowing what a public (untrusted) channel can invoke.\\n\\n**How it's detected:** At least two channels are enabled, the global \`trust.tool_allowlist\` is non-empty, at least one enabled channel is public (\`channels.<name>.public\` — missing defaults to \`true\`/untrusted, same conservative-default posture as CHAP-INJ-001) with no channel-specific \`channels.<name>.tool_allowlist\` override, and at least one enabled channel is private (\`public: false\`). Same manifest-convention caveat as CHAP-AGY-003/004 — no real schema exists for these example agents.\\n\\n**Remediation:** Declare a channel-specific tool_allowlist for each public/untrusted channel, narrower than what private/admin-only channels are permitted to invoke."
