                "text": "The gateway daemon listening on an interface other than localhost (e.g. \`0.0.0.0\`), making it reachable from other hosts.\\n\\nHow it's detected: \`gateway.host\` in config is present and is not a loopback address (\`localhost\`, anything in \`127.0.0.0/8\`, \`::1\`, or IPv4-mapped \`::ffff:127.x.x.x\`). A trailing \`:port\` and \`[...]\` IPv6 brackets are stripped before classifying.\\n\\nRemediation: Bind the gateway to \`127.0.0.1\`/\`localhost\`; put anything that must be reachable remotely behind a tunnel with authentication.",
