            {
              "id": "CHAP-INJ-005",
              "name": "Inbound channels do not distinguish trust level",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Inbound channels do not distinguish trust level"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A non-empty global tool allowlist applied uniformly to a mix of public and private inbound channels, with no channel-specific restriction narrowing what a public (untrusted) channel can invoke."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A non-empty global tool allowlist applied uniformly to a mix of public and private inbound channels, with no channel-specific restriction narrowing what a public (untrusted) channel can invoke.\\n\\nHow it's detected: At least two channels are enabled, the global \`trust.tool_allowlist\` is non-empty, at least one enabled channel is public (\`channels.<name>.public\` — missing defaults to \`true\`/untrusted, same conservative-default posture as CHAP-INJ-001) with no channel-specific \`channels.<name>.tool_allowlist\` override, and at least one enabled channel is private (\`public: false\`). Same manifest-convention caveat as CHAP-AGY-003/004 — no real schema exists for these example agents.\\n\\nRemediation: Declare a channel-specific tool_allowlist for each public/untrusted channel, narrower than what private/admin-only channels are permitted to invoke.",
                "markdown": "A non-empty global tool allowlist applied uniformly to a mix of public and private inbound channels, with no channel-specific restriction narrowing what a public (untrusted) channel can invoke.\\n\\n**How it's detected:** At least two channels are enabled, the global \`trust.tool_allowlist\` is non-empty, at least one enabled channel is public (\`channels.<name>.public\` — missing defaults to \`true\`/untrusted, same conservative-default posture as CHAP-INJ-001) with no channel-specific \`channels.<name>.tool_allowlist\` override, and at least one enabled channel is private (\`public: false\`). Same manifest-convention caveat as CHAP-AGY-003/004 — no real schema exists for these example agents.\\n\\n**Remediation:** Declare a channel-specific tool_allowlist for each public/untrusted channel, narrower than what private/admin-only channels are permitted to invoke."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AlpayAltuntas/chaperone/blob/main/CHECKS.md#chap-inj-005--inbound-channels-do-not-distinguish-trust-level",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "injection",
                "owasp": "LLM01: Prompt Injection",
                "severity": "medium",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "injection"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CHAP-NET-001",
              "name": "Gateway bound beyond localhost",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Gateway bound beyond localhost"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The gateway daemon listening on an interface other than localhost (e.g. \`0.0.0.0\`), making it reachable from other hosts."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The gateway daemon listening on an interface other than localhost (e.g. \`0.0.0.0\`), making it reachable from other hosts.\\n\\nHow it's detected: \`gateway.host\` in config is present and is not a loopback address (\`localhost\`, anything in \`127.0.0.0/8\`, \`::1\`, or IPv4-mapped \`::ffff:127.x.x.x\`). A trailing \`:port\` and \`[...]\` IPv6 brackets are stripped before classifying.\\n\\nRemediation: Bind the gateway to \`127.0.0.1\`/\`localhost\`; put anything that must be reachable remotely behind a tunnel with authentication.",
                "markdown": "The gateway daemon listening on an interface other than localhost (e.g. \`0.0.0.0\`), making it reachable from other hosts.\\n\\n**How it's detected:** \`gateway.host\` in config is present and is not a loopback address (\`localhost\`, anything in \`127.0.0.0/8\`, \`::1\`, or IPv4-mapped \`::ffff:127.x.x.x\`). A trailing \`:port\` and \`[...]\` IPv6 brackets are stripped before classifying.\\n\\n**Remediation:** Bind the gateway to \`127.0.0.1\`/\`localhost\`; put anything that must be reachable remotely behind a tunnel with authentication."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AlpayAltuntas/chaperone/blob/main/CHECKS.md#chap-net-001--gateway-bound-beyond-localhost",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "network",
                "owasp": "LLM06 / general",
                "severity": "critical",
                "security-severity": "9.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "network"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CHAP-NET-002",
              "name": "Missing or weak auth on the gateway control API",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Missing or weak auth on the gateway control API"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The gateway control API with no auth configured, or a weak credential."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The gateway control API with no auth configured, or a weak credential.\\n\\nHow it's detected: \`gateway.auth\` is absent, or its literal \`token\` is empty, a common default (\`changeme\`, \`admin\`, \`password\`, \`default\`, \`token\`, case-insensitive), shorter than 16 characters, or identical to another secret value in the config. An env-var reference (\`\${GW_TOKEN}\`) isn't judged. When \`gateway.host\` is a loopback address, the finding is medium instead of high: there's no network exposure, but local processes and web pages using browser-to-localhost or DNS rebinding can still reach it.\\n\\nRemediation: Require a strong, randomly generated token (at least 16 characters, used nowhere else) for the gateway control API, and rotate any default or reused value.",
                "markdown": "The gateway control API with no auth configured, or a weak credential.\\n\\n**How it's detected:** \`gateway.auth\` is absent, or its literal \`token\` is empty, a common default (\`changeme\`, \`admin\`, \`password\`, \`default\`, \`token\`, case-insensitive), shorter than 16 characters, or identical to another secret value in the config. An env-var reference (\`\${GW_TOKEN}\`) isn't judged. When \`gateway.host\` is a loopback address, the finding is medium instead of high: there's no network exposure, but local processes and web pages using browser-to-localhost or DNS rebinding can still reach it.\\n\\n**Remediation:** Require a strong, randomly generated token (at least 16 characters, used nowhere else) for the gateway control API, and rotate any default or reused value."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AlpayAltuntas/chaperone/blob/main/CHECKS.md#chap-net-002--missing-or-weak-auth-on-the-gateway-control-api",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "network",
                "owasp": "General",
                "severity": "high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "network"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CHAP-NET-003",
              "name": "Plaintext transport on the gateway",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Plaintext transport on the gateway"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The gateway explicitly configured without TLS, or a remote MCP server configured with a plaintext \`http://\` URL."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The gateway explicitly configured without TLS, or a remote MCP server configured with a plaintext \`http://\` URL.\\n\\nHow it's detected: \`gateway.tls\` is explicitly \`false\` (silent when TLS isn't mentioned in config at all: there's no confident signal either way), or a remote MCP server's \`url\` uses \`http://\`/\`ws://\` with a host that isn't loopback (\`localhost\`, \`127.0.0.0/8\`, \`::1\`).\\n\\nRemediation: Enable TLS on the gateway and disable any plaintext fallback.",
                "markdown": "The gateway explicitly configured without TLS, or a remote MCP server configured with a plaintext \`http://\` URL.\\n\\n**How it's detected:** \`gateway.tls\` is explicitly \`false\` (silent when TLS isn't mentioned in config at all: there's no confident signal either way), or a remote MCP server's \`url\` uses \`http://\`/\`ws://\` with a host that isn't loopback (\`localhost\`, \`127.0.0.0/8\`, \`::1\`).\\n\\n**Remediation:** Enable TLS on the gateway and disable any plaintext fallback."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AlpayAltuntas/chaperone/blob/main/CHECKS.md#chap-net-003--plaintext-transport-on-the-gateway",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "network",
                "owasp": "General",
                "severity": "medium",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "network"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CHAP-OBS-001",
              "name": "No audit log of agent actions",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No audit log of agent actions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Tool invocations/actions that aren't logged."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Tool invocations/actions that aren't logged.\\n\\nHow it's detected: \`logging.audit.enabled\` is not \`true\` (covers both an explicitly disabled audit log and no logging config at all).\\n\\nRemediation: Enable an append-only audit log of every tool invocation/action the agent takes.",
                "markdown": "Tool invocations/actions that aren't logged.\\n\\n**How it's detected:** \`logging.audit.enabled\` is not \`true\` (covers both an explicitly disabled audit log and no logging config at all).\\n\\n**Remediation:** Enable an append-only audit log of every tool invocation/action the agent takes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AlpayAltuntas/chaperone/blob/main/CHECKS.md#chap-obs-001--no-audit-log-of-agent-actions",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "observability",
                "owasp": "LLM08-adjacent",
                "severity": "medium",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "observability"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CHAP-OBS-002",
              "name": "Sensitive data in plaintext logs",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Sensitive data in plaintext logs"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Log config that doesn't confirm secrets/message bodies are redacted."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Log config that doesn't confirm secrets/message bodies are redacted.\\n\\nHow it's detected: Logging is configured and \`logging.redact_secrets\` is not \`true\`.\\n\\nRemediation: Redact secrets and sensitive message content before logging, and restrict access to the log file.",
                "markdown": "Log config that doesn't confirm secrets/message bodies are redacted.\\n\\n**How it's detected:** Logging is configured and \`logging.redact_secrets\` is not \`true\`.\\n\\n**Remediation:** Redact secrets and sensitive message content before logging, and restrict access to the log file."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AlpayAltuntas/chaperone/blob/main/CHECKS.md#chap-obs-002--sensitive-data-in-plaintext-logs",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
