            {
              "id": "CHAP-OBS-003",
              "name": "No documented kill switch / revocation path",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No documented kill switch / revocation path"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "No documented quick way to stop the agent and revoke its access."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "No documented quick way to stop the agent and revoke its access.\\n\\nHow it's detected: None of \`KILL_SWITCH.md\`, \`STOP.md\`, \`kill-switch.sh\`, or \`revoke.sh\` exists at the install root — a documented, invented naming convention (no real spec exists for this); an install documenting a kill switch any other way won't be detected in v1.\\n\\nRemediation: Document a kill switch (how to stop the agent) and a script or checklist to revoke/rotate its credentials.",
                "markdown": "No documented quick way to stop the agent and revoke its access.\\n\\n**How it's detected:** None of \`KILL_SWITCH.md\`, \`STOP.md\`, \`kill-switch.sh\`, or \`revoke.sh\` exists at the install root — a documented, invented naming convention (no real spec exists for this); an install documenting a kill switch any other way won't be detected in v1.\\n\\n**Remediation:** Document a kill switch (how to stop the agent) and a script or checklist to revoke/rotate its credentials."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AlpayAltuntas/chaperone/blob/main/CHECKS.md#chap-obs-003--no-documented-kill-switch--revocation-path",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "observability",
                "owasp": "General",
                "severity": "low",
                "security-severity": "3.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "observability"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CHAP-OBS-004",
              "name": "Persistent memory/state store exposed",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Persistent memory/state store exposed"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A configured persistent memory/state directory (one of \`instruction.md\` §2's five discoverable artifacts) that's readable by group/other, or git-tracked and not gitignored."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A configured persistent memory/state directory (one of \`instruction.md\` §2's five discoverable artifacts) that's readable by group/other, or git-tracked and not gitignored.\\n\\nHow it's detected: Mirrors CHAP-SEC-002/CHAP-SEC-003, applied to a \`memory_dir\`/\`state_dir\` config field (mirroring \`skills_dir\`'s existing pattern — see \`discovery/memory.ts\`) instead of the config file. No content inside the directory is ever read; only its existence, permission mode, and git-tracking status. Silent when the directory is configured but doesn't exist on disk.\\n\\nRemediation: Restrict the memory/state directory to owner-only access (chmod 700) and add it to .gitignore — it can accumulate sensitive conversational content over time.",
                "markdown": "A configured persistent memory/state directory (one of \`instruction.md\` §2's five discoverable artifacts) that's readable by group/other, or git-tracked and not gitignored.\\n\\n**How it's detected:** Mirrors CHAP-SEC-002/CHAP-SEC-003, applied to a \`memory_dir\`/\`state_dir\` config field (mirroring \`skills_dir\`'s existing pattern — see \`discovery/memory.ts\`) instead of the config file. No content inside the directory is ever read; only its existence, permission mode, and git-tracking status. Silent when the directory is configured but doesn't exist on disk.\\n\\n**Remediation:** Restrict the memory/state directory to owner-only access (chmod 700) and add it to .gitignore — it can accumulate sensitive conversational content over time."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/AlpayAltuntas/chaperone/blob/main/CHECKS.md#chap-obs-004--persistent-memorystate-store-exposed",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "observability",
                "owasp": "LLM06: Sensitive Information Disclosure",
                "severity": "medium",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "observability"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
